From a07914ad8da3627ecfc17f7825714c758b6eaccf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JerryNee <ni12@illinois.edu>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 16:36:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Add AirPlay 2 mirroring research path behind a profile

Impersonating a system Mac receiver (model=Mac15,6, a modern srcvers and the
HomeKit pairing endpoints) is one way to be offered over Apple peer-to-peer.
It works for discovery, and this adds what that path needs: HomeKit
pair-setup/pair-verify via pair_ap, the encrypted control and event channels,
and the AP2-shaped SETUP handling.

It does not work for video. A sender that sees a Mac receiver switches to the
AP2 media setup, which omits the legacy FairPlay ekey and derives the
mirroring key by a route Apple has not published. Frames arrive and cannot be
decrypted.

Keep it anyway, disabled by default, because it is the only place the AP2
handshake is implemented and because it may matter if senders ever stop
offering the legacy path. Two aids for that work:

- raop_rtp_mirror_add_aes_candidate() decrypts each payload with several
  candidate seeds in parallel and selects whichever produces a valid chain of
  length-prefixed NAL units.

- ap2_capture records the session material a derivation could consume plus
  the first encrypted payloads, so the search can run offline instead of
  spending a physical mirroring session per guess.

Selected by UXPLAY_DISCOVERY_PROFILE=mac-p2p. The shipping configuration does
not use any of this: a plain UxPlay identity reaches AWDL just as well and
keeps the legacy media path that decrypts correctly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
